3. Pre-populated the React Query cache with mock data instead of mocking the API client
4. Kept all the necessary providers (ScopeProvider and QueryClientProvider)
5. Maintained the original component rendering without any modifications

The component should now render properly without the Jest-related error while still maintaining its original functionality and appearance.

